{"items":[{"str":"addressee); how is any given representation about you, speaking to","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,649],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"you or for you, that is, how does it construct you as the consumer of","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,635],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"that representation? This is an easier critical consciousness for some","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,621],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"than for others. For example, as hooks says, there has always been a","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,607],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"tradition of critical consciousness in African American communities in","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,593],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"the United States because of U.S. policies explicitly disenfranchising","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,579],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"such communities. If you know that the dominant culture is not “for”","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,565],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"you or “about” you, it is easier for you to view it with a critical eye. So","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,551],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"too, says hooks, it becomes difficult to be critical of (to critique) a rep-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,537],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"resentation when it is produced by “one of your own” (she gives the","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,523],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"example of Spike Lee), because the representation claims to speak for","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,509],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"you and about you, in your name and in your interests. But whether","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,495],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"the work is easy or hard, critiquing is one of the most important things","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,481],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"to do.","dir":"ltr","width":27,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,467],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,183,467],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"9","dir":"ltr","width":4,"height":7,"transform":[7,0,0,7,183,470],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"We also, all of us, change subject positions. There are times when","dir":"ltr","width":300,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,168,453],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"we will be explicitly “othered” by a representation, just as there are","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,439],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"times when a representation is for us and “others” someone else. The","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,425],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"point is to be aware of this rather than unreflectively responding to it.","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,411],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Here is where the concept of “","dir":"ltr","width":147,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,397],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"interpellation","dir":"ltr","width":65,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,304,397],"fontName":"g_d2896_f1","hasEOL":false},{"str":"” or “hailing,” devel-","dir":"ltr","width":100,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,368,397],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"oped by the French Marxist philosopher Louis Althusser, is very help-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,383],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"ful. It refers to how a social formation constructs us as subjects who","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,369],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"respond and consent to it in certain ways. It is a description of how","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,355],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"ideology functions, not by persuading us with rational argument to","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,341],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"believe that something is true, but by manufacturing our consent to","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,327],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"certain ideas by representing them as self-evident reality.","dir":"ltr","width":250,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,313],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,406,313],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"10","dir":"ltr","width":8,"height":7,"transform":[7,0,0,7,406,316],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"John Fiske’s essay “Cultural Studies and the Culture of Everyday","dir":"ltr","width":300,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,168,299],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Life” introduces some of the key notions in cultural studies: the idea","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,285],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"of culture as the culture of everyday life; the idea of the","dir":"ltr","width":248,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,404,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"habitus","dir":"ltr","width":31,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,407,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,439,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"or so-","dir":"ltr","width":26,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,442,271],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"cial space that locates us in terms of cultural and economic capital, ed-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,257],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"ucation, class, and history (","dir":"ltr","width":124,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"Cultural Studies","dir":"ltr","width":73,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,280,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":", 155). He makes the im-","dir":"ltr","width":115,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,353,243],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"portant point that material, everyday lived culture is a contradictory","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,229],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"mixture of creativity and constraint: “The social order constrains and","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,215],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"oppresses the people, but at the same time offers them resources to","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,201],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"fight against those constraints” (157). Elizabeth Young’s essay “","dir":"ltr","width":296,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,187],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"The","dir":"ltr","width":16,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,452,187],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Silence of the Lambs","dir":"ltr","width":90,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,173],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":" ","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[10,0,0,10,246,173],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"and the Flaying of Feminist Theory” illustrates","dir":"ltr","width":218,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,250,173],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"what Fiske is talking about: how the film offers creative critiques and","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,159],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"possibilities for the questioning of gender even as it constrains and op-","dir":"ltr","width":312,"height":10,"transform":[10,0,0,10,156,145],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,216,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":true},{"str":"Cultural Studies, Popular Culture, and Pedagogy","dir":"ltr","width":191,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,216,677],"fontName":"g_d2896_f3","hasEOL":false},{"str":"","dir":"ltr","width":0,"height":0,"transform":[9,0,0,9,299,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":true},{"str":"| 18 |","dir":"ltr","width":26,"height":9,"transform":[9,0,0,9,299,117],"fontName":"g_d2896_f2","hasEOL":false}],"styles":{"g_d2896_f2":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f1":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.72,"descent":-0.245,"vertical":false},"g_d2896_f3":{"fontFamily":"serif","ascent":0.722,"descent":-0.246,"vertical":false}},"lang":null}